---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { contact, ownerSupplied } from "../data/site";

const description =
  "Terms of use for Straight Up Digital, including service offers, quotes, digital delivery, payments, cancellations and consumer rights.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <section class="legal">
    <div class="container legal__inner">
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
          <p class="legal__meta">Version 1.1 · Last updated 25 November 2026</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          These terms apply to this website. By using it, you agree to them. If you
          do not agree, please stop using the site.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          This website is operated by <strong>{ownerSupplied.legalEntity}</strong>.
          Straight Up Digital is an online-first South African business and a
          trading name, not a registered company.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What this website is for</h2>
        <p>
          The site explains the audit and the services offered, and lets you send an
          enquiry. It is an introduction, not a contract. Any work is governed by a
          separate written proposal or agreement, signed before the work starts.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Information is general</h2>
        <p>
          The content is written in good faith and kept as accurate as practical,
          but it is general information. It is not legal, financial, accounting or
          other professional advice, and it should not be relied on as if it were.
        </p>

        <h2>4. No guarantee of results</h2>
        <p>
          Digital audits are human-reviewed analytical assessments based on
          publicly visible information. They do not measure private analytics,
          guarantee search rankings, traffic volumes or financial returns, and
          are not a promise of a particular business outcome. Search results and
          third-party information can change. Examples are labelled and are not
          client data.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Enquiries and quotes</h2>
        <p>
          Sending the form does not create a contract or oblige either party to
          proceed. A quote is valid for the period stated in it. Work begins only
          after a written scope and quote are accepted. The accepted quote records
          the service, full price, payment schedule, delivery method and timing,
          third-party costs, and any recurring term or renewal price that applies.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Payments, delivery and cancellations</h2>
        <p>
          Enquiry forms on this site do not take payment. A payment is due only
          after you accept a written quote or order and receive an approved payment
          method. Standalone website packages use the stated 50% start and 50%
          launch milestones, with a preview before the launch balance. Discounted
          annual website bundles are paid in full once-off and include the build
          plus the first hosting year; annual hosting renews after that included
          year at the price disclosed in the accepted quote.
        </p>
        <p>
          Digital work is delivered electronically. The accepted quote sets its
          delivery method and timeframe. Physical goods are not shipped through
          this website. For cancellation requests, service delivery, recurring
          renewals and refunds, read our
          <a href="/policies">Delivery, cancellations and refunds policy</a>.
          Nothing in these terms removes rights available under South African law.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The brand, logo, text, layout and images on this site belong to Straight
          Up Digital or are used with permission. You may read, print and share
          pages for your own use. You may not copy the site or the brand into
          another product, or suggest that Straight Up Digital endorses it, without
          written permission.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          The site may link to third-party websites, such as hosting or platform
          documentation. Those sites are not under our control and their terms and
          privacy notices apply.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Availability</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to keep the site available and correct, but we do not promise
          uninterrupted access. Maintenance, hosting problems or security work may
          take it offline temporarily.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent the law allows, Straight Up Digital is not liable for loss
          caused by relying on general information on this site, by a third-party
          site we link to, or by the site being temporarily unavailable. Nothing in
          these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
        </p>
        <h2>11. Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Personal information is handled as described in the{" "}
          <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of South Africa. Any dispute will
          be dealt with by a court with jurisdiction under South African law.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may change. The version date at the top will change with
          them. Continued use of the site after a change means you accept the new
          version.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms can be sent to{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> or through the{" "}
          <a href="/contact">enquiry form</a>.
        </p>
        <p>Service area: PROUDLY SOUTH AFRICAN. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
